# 7. Linux Service and Log Management

## `systemctl`

Used to inspect and manage systemd services.

Example:

```bash
systemctl status ssh
```

## `journalctl`

Used to view logs collected by the systemd journal.

Example:

```bash
journalctl -u ssh
```

### Concept

```text
systemctl
↓
Service Management

journalctl
↓
Logs
```

