# 18. Tool Selection

Today's training reinforced choosing tools based on symptoms.

| Problem                  | Appropriate Tool       |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------- |
| Slow Windows computer    | Task Manager           |
| Windows service          | `services.msc`         |
| Application/system error | Event Viewer           |
| Hardware/driver issue    | Device Manager         |
| Startup issue            | `msconfig`             |
| GPO issue                | `gpupdate`, `gpresult` |
| IP configuration         | `ipconfig /all`        |
| DNS issue                | `nslookup`             |
| Network path             | `tracert`              |
| Linux process            | `ps`, `top`, `htop`    |
| Linux disk               | `df -h`                |
| Linux memory             | `free -h`              |
| Linux service            | `systemctl`            |
| Linux service logs       | `journalctl`           |

### Key principle

> Choose the troubleshooting tool based on the symptom and the information you need to collect.

